\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, teach us how to pray aright,
\par With reverence and with fear;
\par Though dust and ashes in Thy sight,
\par We may, we must draw near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. We perish if we cease from prayer;
\par O grant us powerto pray!
\par And when to meet Thee we prepare,
\par Lord, meet us by the way.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Give deep humility; the sense
\par Of godly sorrow give;
\par A strong desiring confidence
\par To hear Thy voice and live;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Faith in the only sacrifice
\par That can for sin atone;
\par To build our hopes, to fix our eyes,
\par On Christ, on Christ alone;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Patience to watch, and wait, and weep,
\par Though mercy long delay;
\par Courage, our fainting souls to keep
\par And trust Thee, though Thou slay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Give these, and then, Thy will be done:
\par Thus strengthen with all might,
\par We through Thy Spirit and Thy Son
\par Shall pray, and pray aright.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

